    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5274" root="جدى" body-key="j">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَدَيْتُهُ</span></b> : see 1 in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جدو</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  One says of
the locust, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَجْدِى كُلَّ شَىْءٍ</span>, meaning <i>It eats
everything.</i> (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَمْ أَجْدِ مِنْ ذٰلِكَ بُدًّا</span> <i>I
found no means of avoiding,</i> or <i>escaping, that,</i>
is sometimes said for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَمْ أَجِدْ الخ??</span>. (Kz, TA in
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وجد</span>.)

